A1. The kind of son that shines. ~ SMART
A5. She can't play this if she won't hold hands. ~ POKER
A9. This is always fatal. ~ FATE
A11. To postpone. ~ DEFER
A13. This fellow saw two of everything on water. ~ NOAH
A16. A man who has the goods on him. ~ AGENT
A18. Good for a holdup. ~ PIN
A19. To worship. ~ ADORE
A20. Give and take. ~ SWAP
A21. What love would be if it lasted for ever and ever. ~ ETERNAL
A24. Something to get caught on. ~ TRAP
A26. This is as busy as a bee. ~ ANT
A27. This is always in this place. ~ HERE
A28. A part of any good egg. ~ YOLK
A30. This is always monkeying around. ~ APE
A31. The best in France, if not Fifth avenue. ~ ELITE
A33. Cowboys are supposed to be this. ~ RANGY
A35. A suffix. ~ ES
A37. Pains-in-the-neck. ~ ACHES
A39. A ticket to dreamland. ~ ETHER
A40. In this or that manner. ~ SO
A41. What some skunk did in Herrin, Ill. ~ SIUNK
A43. This never changes at Dayton, Tenn. ~ DOGMA
A45. This is always on the house. ~ EAVES
A47. What is the Venus de Milo? ~ ART
A48. The right stick to use on an approach (ask the ladies). ~ LIP
A49. This has a lot of crust. ~ PIE
A50. What Samson lost with a haircut. ~ SINEW
A52. This always comes before the tenth of the month. ~ NINTH
A54. The sun never shines where this is. ~ SHADE
A56. An article. ~ AN
A57. This is very swift. ~ RAPID
A59. A well-red man from Mexico. ~ YAQUI
A61. A new one January 1st (abbr.). ~ YR
