A63. A dumb one. ~ DUNCE
A65. The cat's whiskers. ~ AWN
A67. You can't do this with your eyes shut. ~ PEEK
A69. The kind of end a business man prefers. ~ WEEK
A70. Very tall and wears a white cap. ~ ALP
A72. The sweetie—what you call her and what she is. ~ DEAR
A74. This can be given and kept at the same time (handle with care—breakable). ~ PROMISE
A76. Collegiate club (abbr.). ~ FRAT
A77. Social Register full of them. ~ SNOBS
A79. The way to get to Washington. ~ RUN
A80. These have to be hit over the head to get anywhere. ~ NAILS
A82. The rent. ~ TEAR
A83. A golf instructor. ~ CADDY
A85. Famous Lady Yegg Society (init.). ~ FLYS
A86. Anyone who disagrees with you. ~ MORON
A87. This is always a hit. ~ SMITE

D1. You should watch this in Chicago. ~ STEP
D2. These are often lit at stag parties. ~ MEN
D3. An open way (abbr.). ~ RD
D4. This used to be raised in this country by the Indians. ~ TEPEE
D5. Often asked for people's thoughts—and rarely ever worth the price. ~ PENNY
